# Python Virtual Environment

This project uses a local venv at `.venv/`. Do **not** rely on system `PATH` or assume `python` resolves correctly.

## Before Python Commands

**MANDATORY:** Activate the venv before `python`, `pytest`, `pip`, `uv`, or any project script.

```powershell
& c:/Sources/ViralAutomation/.venv/Scripts/Activate.ps1
```

Then run commands normally:

```powershell
python -m pytest tests/
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## One-Off Commands

Chain activation in the same shell invocation:

```powershell
& c:/Sources/ViralAutomation/.venv/Scripts/Activate.ps1; python -m pytest tests/test_transcribe.py
```

## Persistent Shell Sessions

- Activate **once** at the start of a new terminal session.
- Re-activate if the shell was reset or a new terminal was opened.
- Do not skip activation because a prior command "probably" used the right Python.

## Subagents

Include this rule in every subagent prompt that runs Python, pytest, pip, or project CLI tools.

## Avoid

- Calling bare `python` without activating first
- Using `py` launcher or system Python when project venv exists
- Assuming `PYTHONPATH` or IDE settings initialized the environment
